135
00:06:11,140 --> 00:06:12,580
He blew a golden opportunity.

136
00:06:14,080 --> 00:06:15,700
Huh? He texted again.

137
00:06:16,200 --> 00:06:17,220
Maybe another pic?

138
00:06:17,220 --> 00:06:23,460
What did he send?

139
00:06:26,500 --> 00:06:28,660
I guess that he wants to meet me.

140
00:06:28,960 --> 00:06:31,240
But right now? Right now, right now?

141
00:06:31,660 --> 00:06:33,160
What am I going to do?

142
00:06:35,120 --> 00:06:36,180
You'll figure it out. Go.

143
00:06:36,740 --> 00:06:37,140
What?

144
00:06:37,380 --> 00:06:39,140
But Owen, I can't leave you all alone.

145
00:06:39,140 --> 00:06:42,220
I have an important live stream to watch, and I cannot be disturbed.

146
00:06:42,400 --> 00:06:42,720
Go.

147
00:06:42,880 --> 00:06:43,320
Oh, okay.

148
00:06:44,820 --> 00:06:45,840
Yo, wait up.

149
00:06:48,600 --> 00:06:52,260
I wasn't expecting so many people to be wandering around the hotel.

150
00:06:53,860 --> 00:06:54,860
There he is.

151
00:06:57,460 --> 00:06:59,740
Looks like other girls are chatting with him.

152
00:07:00,420 --> 00:07:00,900
Wait.

153
00:07:01,360 --> 00:07:03,980
Am I not the only one he texted about meeting up tonight?

154
00:07:04,320 --> 00:07:05,320
I guess it's possible.

155
00:07:05,320 --> 00:07:07,480
Oh, they're leaving.

156
00:07:08,280 --> 00:07:09,720
I know someone else is coming.

157
00:07:10,620 --> 00:07:13,380
I thought people only greeted each other like that on TV.

158
00:07:14,160 --> 00:07:18,140
Come to think of it, Yamada does hang out with girls pretty often.

159
00:07:19,100 --> 00:07:19,520
Uh-oh.

160
00:07:21,080 --> 00:07:24,120
All this time, Yamada has been really friendly to me,

161
00:07:24,240 --> 00:07:26,700
and I've been taking it as a sign that he likes me.

162
00:07:26,940 --> 00:07:29,340
It turns my brain into goop every time.

163
00:07:29,960 --> 00:07:30,460
But wait.

164
00:07:30,840 --> 00:07:33,840
What if this is all an embarrassing misunderstanding on my part?

165
00:07:33,840 --> 00:07:36,080
Like this is something that never happens to me,

166
00:07:36,180 --> 00:07:38,180
but for Yamada, it's just another day.

167
00:07:38,680 --> 00:07:39,700
What do I do?

168
00:07:39,880 --> 00:07:41,120
I'm so inexperienced,

169
00:07:41,180 --> 00:07:43,900
I never thought to take a step back and question it all.

170
00:07:44,040 --> 00:07:44,400
Hey.

171
00:07:45,080 --> 00:07:46,260
How come you didn't say hi?

172
00:07:48,660 --> 00:07:49,100
Oh.

173
00:07:50,100 --> 00:07:52,280
You were busy with other people earlier.

174
00:07:52,620 --> 00:07:53,760
Then more people after that.

175
00:07:53,780 --> 00:07:54,080
Ah.

176
00:07:54,340 --> 00:07:55,680
Didn't want anybody to see us?

177
00:07:57,060 --> 00:07:57,500
Maybe.

178
00:07:58,300 --> 00:07:59,320
This is bad.

179
00:07:59,540 --> 00:08:00,660
I'm getting all subconscious.

180
00:08:01,160 --> 00:08:02,300
Yeah, I totally feel ya.

181
00:08:02,300 --> 00:08:04,800
It's too crowded here.

182
00:08:07,300 --> 00:08:07,740
Hmm.

183
00:08:08,320 --> 00:08:08,780
Come on.

184
00:08:09,340 --> 00:08:11,140
Let's go find a spot to chat by ourselves.

185
00:08:11,140 --> 00:08:22,640
All the paranoid theories that were running wild in my mind just melted away in a second.

186
00:08:30,640 --> 00:08:33,900
Yamada's words and actions are always so straightforward.

187
00:08:34,620 --> 00:08:36,060
He says what he means.

188
00:08:36,060 --> 00:08:40,200
Oh, did you see this cat over by Kinkaku-ji?

189
00:08:40,360 --> 00:08:41,540
Oh, I didn't.

190
00:08:41,860 --> 00:08:42,900
It's so cute.

191
00:08:43,520 --> 00:08:44,460
Here's Taira.

192
00:08:44,580 --> 00:08:45,840
That guy I told you about.

193
00:08:46,060 --> 00:08:48,200
Oh, I think I've seen him around before.

194
00:08:48,600 --> 00:08:50,020
And this is Azuma.

195
00:08:50,300 --> 00:08:51,340
She's very pretty.

196
00:08:51,700 --> 00:08:52,780
The big guy's Morimo.

197
00:08:53,280 --> 00:08:53,720
Morimo?

198
00:08:53,720 --> 00:08:56,760
Oh, bath time.

199
00:08:57,320 --> 00:08:58,540
I should probably sit back.

200
00:08:59,040 --> 00:09:00,540
Yeah, I should too.

201
00:09:05,040 --> 00:09:05,480
Nishi?

202
00:09:05,680 --> 00:09:05,820
Huh?

203
00:09:07,020 --> 00:09:08,580
Do you want to hang out later?

204
00:09:08,920 --> 00:09:10,200
Like after the class trip?

205
00:09:10,740 --> 00:09:11,040
Huh?

206
00:09:11,040 --> 00:09:15,320
I just really want to take you somewhere quiet and chill.

207
00:09:15,920 --> 00:09:16,760
Anywhere you want.

208
00:09:17,720 --> 00:09:18,420
What do you say?

209
00:09:21,040 --> 00:09:21,560
Okay.

210
00:09:22,840 --> 00:09:24,040
What should I do?

211
00:09:24,040 --> 00:09:24,120
Oh.

212
00:09:31,500 --> 00:09:36,040
There's so much I don't understand about the way Yamada feels and acts, but...

213
00:09:36,040 --> 00:09:40,140
You know I can't stand when people tiptoe around the truth.

214
00:09:41,400 --> 00:09:43,520
I need to be honest with myself.

215
00:09:44,480 --> 00:09:46,580
I can't push my feelings down anymore.

216
00:09:49,260 --> 00:09:50,440
I like him.

217
00:09:54,760 --> 00:09:56,260
Nothing beats bed rot.

218
00:09:56,260 --> 00:10:03,500
Back in middle school, I was too lame to say I didn't want to go on my class trip.

219
00:10:04,100 --> 00:10:08,260
So along I went, counting down the hours until it ended and I could go home.

220
00:10:09,540 --> 00:10:11,440
But nah, it's different.

221
00:10:11,440 --> 00:10:25,460
Surprising as it may seem, I'm having fun.

222
00:10:25,920 --> 00:10:26,840
A lot of fun.

223
00:10:27,740 --> 00:10:29,480
Freeze the day on day three!

224
00:10:29,920 --> 00:10:31,680
Time for class activities.

225
00:10:35,920 --> 00:10:36,480
Teacher!

226
00:10:37,040 --> 00:10:38,700
My stomach wants ice cream!

227
00:10:39,420 --> 00:10:39,940
Seriously?

228
00:10:40,400 --> 00:10:40,680
Huh?

229
00:10:40,680 --> 00:10:41,600
Yeah, go ahead.

230
00:10:41,700 --> 00:10:42,540
You're cool with that?

231
00:10:43,100 --> 00:10:45,080
Oh yeah, I mean, we're pretty ahead of schedule.

232
00:10:45,360 --> 00:10:46,300
Oh, hundo pee!

233
00:10:46,400 --> 00:10:47,840
We're breezing past the other classes.

234
00:10:48,020 --> 00:10:48,940
Eat our dust!

235
00:10:49,540 --> 00:10:53,400
As long as you make it back to the bus before it leaves, feel free to run off wherever.

236
00:10:53,660 --> 00:10:54,020
Yeah!

237
00:10:56,420 --> 00:10:57,300
All right!

238
00:10:59,420 --> 00:11:00,140
What's funny?

239
00:11:00,980 --> 00:11:01,460
Nothing.

240
00:11:02,100 --> 00:11:03,520
Stop looking at me like that.

241
00:11:03,940 --> 00:11:04,340
Huh.

242
00:11:04,340 --> 00:11:10,440
After breaking free of the past, there have been times where I almost let my excitement show.

243
00:11:10,440 --> 00:11:14,120
And when I sense that it's about to escape, I push it back down.

244
00:11:14,900 --> 00:11:16,460
Especially when I'm with Azuma.

245
00:11:17,120 --> 00:11:18,700
It's the perfect recipe for...

246
00:11:20,220 --> 00:11:22,620
Crippling self-consciousness and self-loathing.

247
00:11:23,160 --> 00:11:23,460
Whoa.

248
00:11:23,760 --> 00:11:24,580
Where'd that come from?

249
00:11:25,580 --> 00:11:26,100
Ooh!

250
00:11:26,220 --> 00:11:26,840
Wait a sec!

251
00:11:26,900 --> 00:11:28,680
I'm gonna buy some deal tweets first!

252
00:11:28,680 --> 00:11:30,460
It looks like there's enough to share.

253
00:11:31,240 --> 00:11:31,720
Cutie!

254
00:11:31,760 --> 00:11:33,140
What's wrong?

255
00:11:33,620 --> 00:11:34,100
Nothing.

256
00:11:34,620 --> 00:11:36,900
Hey, Tida, wanna go halfsies on a pack with me?

257
00:11:37,520 --> 00:11:38,220
I have fun.

258
00:11:41,180 --> 00:11:41,660
Whoa!

259
00:11:41,780 --> 00:11:42,960
Why are they super bottles?

260
00:11:43,180 --> 00:11:44,580
How do you not feed those mugs?

261
00:11:47,040 --> 00:11:48,220
What are the time, besties?

262
00:11:48,920 --> 00:11:49,220
Ow!

263
00:11:49,740 --> 00:11:51,060
Eat the cracker, not my hand!

264
00:11:51,780 --> 00:11:52,160
Gah!

265
00:11:52,360 --> 00:11:52,900
Ear spit!

266
00:11:53,460 --> 00:11:54,500
Simmer down, guys.

267
00:11:54,720 --> 00:11:55,880
Hey, you got one earlier!

268
00:11:56,160 --> 00:11:56,920
No seconds, bro!

269
00:11:57,220 --> 00:11:57,760
Stop it!

270
00:11:58,180 --> 00:12:00,200
Yamada's a real deer whisperer, ain't he?

271
00:12:00,520 --> 00:12:01,720
You guys!

272
00:12:02,240 --> 00:12:05,880
The deer ate all my treats and then they just left like it meant nothing!

273
00:12:06,080 --> 00:12:06,340
Hey!

274
00:12:06,460 --> 00:12:08,400
Tida's empty-handed and they still love him.

275
00:12:08,900 --> 00:12:09,720
Oh, Alexei!

276
00:12:10,320 --> 00:12:12,200
You fucking Casanova!

277
00:12:13,740 --> 00:12:15,980
Stop laughing and help me get out of here!

278
00:12:24,020 --> 00:12:24,500
Huh?

279
00:12:25,880 --> 00:12:28,760
Hello!

280
00:12:29,140 --> 00:12:31,000
If we could have your attention up here, please!

281
00:12:31,260 --> 00:12:33,100
It's time for an important PSA!

282
00:12:33,880 --> 00:12:35,700
We're turning this sucker into a party blast!

283
00:12:35,880 --> 00:12:37,380
So if you're ready to arrange, say yeah!

284
00:12:38,060 --> 00:12:38,620
Yeah!

285
00:12:39,440 --> 00:12:41,600
We are not at a concert, sit down!

286
00:12:41,820 --> 00:12:44,180
Shout out to my guy, Tani, in the front row!

287
00:12:44,620 --> 00:12:46,260
He is parsec!

288
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:48,800
MC, more like TMI.

289
00:12:49,560 --> 00:12:49,960
Tida!

290
00:12:50,260 --> 00:12:50,420
Huh?

291
00:12:51,260 --> 00:12:52,160
Over here!

292
00:12:52,160 --> 00:12:54,580
You know what I think it's time for?

293
00:12:54,820 --> 00:12:56,400
Let's play a little riddle game!

294
00:12:56,660 --> 00:12:58,000
Question number one!

295
00:12:59,040 --> 00:12:59,640
Okay, people!

296
00:13:00,040 --> 00:13:02,540
Does anybody know what you've got to do with the snacks I bought today?

297
00:13:03,540 --> 00:13:04,680
Alright, pee our teeth?

298
00:13:05,180 --> 00:13:07,380
Those kind of remind me of our trip in elementary school.

299
00:13:07,880 --> 00:13:08,540
Time flies.

300
00:13:08,960 --> 00:13:10,080
Nabe recommended them.

301
00:13:10,080 --> 00:13:13,280
You got some kind of problem with the nabe, sweet tooth?

302
00:13:13,500 --> 00:13:15,080
Turn back around before we hit a bump.

303
00:13:16,160 --> 00:13:17,380
Ooh, roulette!

304
00:13:17,640 --> 00:13:19,080
You never know if it's sour or sweet.

305
00:13:19,460 --> 00:13:20,560
You can have it.

306
00:13:20,700 --> 00:13:21,640
Just tell me what you get.

307
00:13:22,040 --> 00:13:22,400
Here.

308
00:13:22,400 --> 00:13:24,300
I don't get it.

309
00:13:24,460 --> 00:13:26,500
Boy, it's a pine, you bird brain.

310
00:13:26,900 --> 00:13:27,140
Oh.

311
00:13:28,360 --> 00:13:29,040
It's sour.

312
00:13:29,580 --> 00:13:30,740
I'm not even phased.

313
00:13:30,920 --> 00:13:32,060
I said it's sour.

314
00:13:32,780 --> 00:13:33,860
What do you want from me?

315
00:13:33,980 --> 00:13:36,460
What does a helpful bird do when there's a problem?

316
00:13:36,860 --> 00:13:37,040
Oh?

317
00:13:37,660 --> 00:13:38,400
Back here!

318
00:13:38,840 --> 00:13:39,280
Oh!

319
00:13:39,440 --> 00:13:40,500
An active participant!

320
00:13:40,780 --> 00:13:41,500
Hit me, Zuma girl!

321
00:13:41,960 --> 00:13:43,000
They squawk it out?

322
00:13:43,500 --> 00:13:44,140
And...

323
00:13:44,140 --> 00:13:44,580
Incorrect!

324
00:13:44,600 --> 00:13:45,720
Wow, she got it wrong.

325
00:13:45,980 --> 00:13:46,800
Oh, really?

326
00:13:47,280 --> 00:13:49,060
I so thought I nailed that one.

327
00:13:50,060 --> 00:13:51,140
I did it.

328
00:13:51,140 --> 00:13:52,840
And what's that look?

329
00:13:53,160 --> 00:13:54,200
You disappointed in me?

330
00:13:54,560 --> 00:13:54,860
What?

331
00:13:55,160 --> 00:13:55,700
No, dude.

332
00:13:56,080 --> 00:13:57,520
It's just...

333
00:13:57,520 --> 00:13:59,080
Was Zuma always like this?

334
00:14:04,400 --> 00:14:05,660
Oh, Tani.

335
00:14:05,940 --> 00:14:06,740
You okay, man?

336
00:14:07,060 --> 00:14:08,780
You don't want to miss dinner, my dude!

337
00:14:09,080 --> 00:14:10,900
All you can eat, eat, eat, me, me, me!

338
00:14:11,520 --> 00:14:13,340
Don't talk about food right now, dude.

339
00:14:13,960 --> 00:14:15,000
Go on without me.

340
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:16,560
I just want some fresh air.

341
00:14:17,100 --> 00:14:17,980
R.I.P. bro.

342
00:14:18,360 --> 00:14:20,340
If you have trouble finding us, call me.

343
00:14:20,340 --> 00:14:21,380
Thank you.

344
00:14:22,220 --> 00:14:22,660
Lame?

345
00:14:22,800 --> 00:14:25,080
Of course this is the one time I ran out of tea.

346
00:14:25,320 --> 00:14:26,020
That's all right.

347
00:14:26,380 --> 00:14:26,940
Thank you.

348
00:14:32,060 --> 00:14:33,700
Wow, soda before a buffet?

349
00:14:36,340 --> 00:14:37,140
Chill out.

350
00:14:37,260 --> 00:14:37,960
It's just me.

351
00:14:38,800 --> 00:14:40,220
It's not for me.

352
00:14:40,220 --> 00:14:43,860
I read somewhere online soda can help settle an upset stomach.

353
00:14:43,860 --> 00:14:48,480
Okay, now it's your turn to chill out.

354
00:14:49,320 --> 00:14:51,980
Do you usually get carsick on longer trips like that?

355
00:14:52,500 --> 00:14:53,120
I don't.

356
00:14:53,440 --> 00:14:54,700
I'm normally just fine.

357
00:14:54,940 --> 00:14:55,540
That was weird.

358
00:14:55,980 --> 00:14:57,280
But I do feel better now.

359
00:14:57,820 --> 00:14:58,960
That's such a relief.

360
00:14:59,280 --> 00:15:03,300
Though maybe you weren't feeling good in the first place, and we still have one more day left.

361
00:15:03,580 --> 00:15:04,300
I'll be fine.

362
00:15:05,020 --> 00:15:05,380
Good.

363
00:15:05,860 --> 00:15:08,620
It's gonna get chilly soon, so I should start heading back.

364
00:15:13,140 --> 00:15:15,160
Can you stay a bit longer?

365
00:15:18,940 --> 00:15:19,340
Okay.

366
00:15:19,340 --> 00:15:36,900
Sick?

367
00:15:37,060 --> 00:15:37,720
Yeah, right.

368
00:15:37,860 --> 00:15:38,840
I brought him a soda.

369
00:15:38,840 --> 00:15:43,240
I almost got back there.

370
00:15:43,600 --> 00:15:45,900
People really talk like that in real life?

371
00:15:46,620 --> 00:15:48,040
It's so cute and awkward.

372
00:15:48,140 --> 00:15:48,740
It's hilarious.

373
00:15:48,760 --> 00:15:51,180
I need to wash my eyes out with boiling water.

374
00:15:51,800 --> 00:15:52,580
Whatever, though.

375
00:15:52,620 --> 00:15:54,000
At least I've got some cola now.

376
00:15:57,280 --> 00:15:58,760
What the hell?

377
00:15:59,280 --> 00:15:59,800
Seriously?

378
00:16:02,600 --> 00:16:06,700
This is funny to you, me being in pain.

379
00:16:06,700 --> 00:16:09,060
Sorry, but your face is so funny.

380
00:16:16,060 --> 00:16:16,660
You know, Asuma?

381
00:16:17,800 --> 00:16:18,700
You really...

382
00:16:19,300 --> 00:16:22,320
You really are my classmate.

383
00:16:28,780 --> 00:16:29,260
Huh?

384
00:16:29,540 --> 00:16:30,460
Of course I am.

385
00:16:30,960 --> 00:16:31,940
I mean, what?

386
00:16:33,660 --> 00:16:35,860
We're in the same class together this year,

387
00:16:35,860 --> 00:16:39,260
and we were in the same class together last year, too, right?

388
00:16:39,560 --> 00:16:39,960
So...

389
00:16:39,960 --> 00:16:40,860
Yeah, I mean...

390
00:16:41,880 --> 00:16:43,260
We were, but...

391
00:16:43,260 --> 00:16:46,740
I wanted to tell her that she's really changed somehow.

392
00:16:47,240 --> 00:16:49,680
Why did I say that, stupid stupid?

393
00:16:51,120 --> 00:16:51,600
Huh?

394
00:16:51,860 --> 00:16:52,800
I can't move!

395
00:16:53,220 --> 00:16:54,140
Why can't I move?

396
00:16:54,520 --> 00:16:56,160
He paralyzed me with his cuteness!

397
00:16:56,160 --> 00:16:57,060
Why can't I go back?

398
00:16:57,060 --> 00:17:01,560
Why can't I go back?

399
00:17:01,560 --> 00:17:02,140
Free time!

400
00:17:02,200 --> 00:17:02,560
I can't!

401
00:17:06,560 --> 00:17:08,620
Which one should we ride first?

402
00:17:08,760 --> 00:17:10,540
We gotta move fast if we want to park, Max.

403
00:17:11,120 --> 00:17:12,780
Don't you have a date to go on?

404
00:17:12,840 --> 00:17:13,460
Get lost.

405
00:17:13,700 --> 00:17:14,520
That was blunt.

406
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:16,360
Enjoy your date, Suzuki.

407
00:17:16,660 --> 00:17:18,900
If we run into you, we'll pretend you're a stranger.

408
00:17:18,900 --> 00:17:20,900
Okay, you don't have to be rude about it.

409
00:17:20,900 --> 00:17:23,900
They say that couples tend to argue at amusement parks,

410
00:17:23,900 --> 00:17:24,900
so best of luck to you.

411
00:17:24,900 --> 00:17:26,900
Thanks, Nabe. You have fun too.

412
00:17:26,900 --> 00:17:29,900
If a long line makes a dude you're with get all grumpy and lame,

413
00:17:29,900 --> 00:17:31,900
you should assume you're finally witnessing their true nature,

414
00:17:31,900 --> 00:17:32,900
for better or for worse.

415
00:17:32,900 --> 00:17:34,900
I hope that's not from experience.

416
00:17:36,900 --> 00:17:37,900
Where to first?

417
00:17:37,900 --> 00:17:40,900
Ooh! Let's make a stop straight ahead!

418
00:17:40,900 --> 00:17:43,900
Just what we need, a popcorn bucket!

419
00:17:43,900 --> 00:17:45,900
So I can walk and talk and munch all at once!

420
00:17:45,900 --> 00:17:47,900
Isn't you, darling?

421
00:17:47,900 --> 00:17:48,900
Darling?

422
00:17:48,900 --> 00:17:53,900
If you say so.

423
00:17:53,900 --> 00:17:56,900
Let's take a look at some hats, too!

424
00:17:56,900 --> 00:17:59,900
Oh! They're all so adorable!

425
00:17:59,900 --> 00:18:01,900
Huh?

426
00:18:05,900 --> 00:18:08,900
Huh. That's a bold choice for him.

427
00:18:08,900 --> 00:18:11,900
This one...seems like you.

428
00:18:11,900 --> 00:18:14,900
Seems like me?

429
00:18:14,900 --> 00:18:16,900
Like it'd look good on me?

430
00:18:16,900 --> 00:18:17,900
A key!

431
00:18:17,900 --> 00:18:21,900
In that case, let's find one that would look good on my mane!

432
00:18:21,900 --> 00:18:22,900
Uh...

433
00:18:22,900 --> 00:18:23,900
No, I don't need one.

434
00:18:23,900 --> 00:18:24,900
Huh?

435
00:18:24,900 --> 00:18:25,900
Oh!

436
00:18:25,900 --> 00:18:26,900
Ah!

437
00:18:26,900 --> 00:18:27,900
Yes, sir!

438
00:18:27,900 --> 00:18:28,900
That was close!

439
00:18:28,900 --> 00:18:30,900
The Suzuki blinders were almost engaged!

440
00:18:30,900 --> 00:18:35,900
If I get too carried away, I'm gonna walk out of here looking like the rat king of crane machine prizes!

441
00:18:35,900 --> 00:18:40,900
But again, I low-key wanna get at least some matching something with Tani!

442
00:18:40,900 --> 00:18:41,900
Is that too much to ask?

443
00:18:41,900 --> 00:18:43,900
I guess that's not really his thing.

444
00:18:43,900 --> 00:18:44,900
Oh.

445
00:18:44,900 --> 00:18:45,900
Hmm?

446
00:18:45,900 --> 00:18:46,900
Let's get a pair.

447
00:18:46,900 --> 00:18:47,900
Like we did before.

448
00:18:47,900 --> 00:18:48,900
A tradition.

449
00:18:48,900 --> 00:18:49,900
Yay!

450
00:18:49,900 --> 00:18:59,900
So merch like this is fine, but headwear is a hard nope.

451
00:18:59,900 --> 00:19:03,900
I mean, it's hard to imagine myself wearing things like that on my head.

452
00:19:03,900 --> 00:19:06,900
They'd look good on you, but they'd look weird on me.

453
00:19:06,900 --> 00:19:08,900
Nah, you wouldn't look weird!

454
00:19:08,900 --> 00:19:13,900
Besides, in a place like this, you have to let your freak flag fly, or you'll regret it forever.

455
00:19:13,900 --> 00:19:14,900
Right.

456
00:19:14,900 --> 00:19:18,900
It's we've got breaking you out of that shell, little crabby crab!

457
00:19:18,900 --> 00:19:19,900
Mmmmm.

458
00:19:19,900 --> 00:19:20,900
Hahaha!

459
00:19:20,900 --> 00:19:21,900
It's fine!

460
00:19:21,900 --> 00:19:23,900
Don't force yourself on my account!

461
00:19:23,900 --> 00:19:24,900
Hmmmm.

462
00:19:27,900 --> 00:19:28,900
Huh?

463
00:19:28,900 --> 00:19:29,900
Want some popcorn?

464
00:19:29,900 --> 00:19:30,900
Voila!

465
00:19:30,900 --> 00:19:31,900
Thank you.

466
00:19:35,900 --> 00:19:36,900
Mmmmm.

467
00:19:36,900 --> 00:19:40,900
For some reason, it really is starting to look cute to me.

468
00:19:40,900 --> 00:19:41,900
What?

469
00:19:41,900 --> 00:19:42,900
You didn't think I was cute before?

470
00:19:42,900 --> 00:19:43,900
You didn't think I was cute before?

471
00:19:56,900 --> 00:19:58,900
This day is perfecto!

472
00:19:59,900 --> 00:20:04,900
Nabe and the gals made it sound like we were bound to bicker today, getting all antsy with the long wait times.

473
00:20:05,900 --> 00:20:07,900
But you'd have to try not to have fun here.

474
00:20:09,900 --> 00:20:10,900
It is fun.

475
00:20:11,900 --> 00:20:14,900
Although, I think we're out of time to do much else.

476
00:20:14,900 --> 00:20:15,900
It's already that late?

477
00:20:15,900 --> 00:20:16,900
Hm?

478
00:20:18,900 --> 00:20:19,900
Oh!

479
00:20:19,900 --> 00:20:20,900
Asu just texted!

480
00:20:21,900 --> 00:20:23,900
Aw, looks like everyone else is together!

481
00:20:24,900 --> 00:20:26,900
I guess we should catch up with the party.

482
00:20:27,900 --> 00:20:31,900
Boy, time sure flies when you're having fun, am I right?

483
00:20:31,900 --> 00:20:32,900
Mio.

484
00:20:32,900 --> 00:20:33,900
Wait.

485
00:20:33,900 --> 00:20:34,900
Yusuke?

486
00:20:34,900 --> 00:20:35,900
Um…

487
00:20:35,900 --> 00:20:37,900
Could we… take the long way there?

488
00:20:37,900 --> 00:20:38,900
Hey…

489
00:20:38,900 --> 00:20:39,900
What's going on?

490
00:20:39,900 --> 00:20:40,900
Today…

491
00:20:40,900 --> 00:20:41,900
You've been so…

492
00:20:41,900 --> 00:20:42,900
Actually yesterday too…

493
00:20:42,900 --> 00:20:43,900
And before that even…

494
00:20:43,900 --> 00:20:44,900
Are you gonna kill me?

495
00:20:44,900 --> 00:20:45,900
What?

496
00:20:45,900 --> 00:20:46,900
No…

497
00:20:46,900 --> 00:20:47,900
Have I been different?

498
00:20:47,900 --> 00:20:48,900
I guess…

499
00:20:48,900 --> 00:20:49,900
Maybe this is me?

500
00:20:49,900 --> 00:20:50,900
I guess…

501
00:20:51,900 --> 00:20:52,900
Maybe this is…

502
00:20:52,900 --> 00:20:54,900
Take the long way there.

503
00:20:57,720 --> 00:21:00,360
Hey, what's going on?

504
00:21:00,820 --> 00:21:03,900
Today, you've been so...

505
00:21:04,440 --> 00:21:05,920
Actually, yesterday, too.

506
00:21:06,840 --> 00:21:07,980
And before that, even.

507
00:21:09,040 --> 00:21:10,520
Are you gonna kill me?

508
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:11,860
What? No.

509
00:21:13,120 --> 00:21:14,440
Have I been different?

510
00:21:15,120 --> 00:21:15,900
I guess...

511
00:21:17,260 --> 00:21:19,400
Maybe this is me getting a little weird.

512
00:21:20,700 --> 00:21:22,600
What kind of laugh was that?

513
00:21:22,900 --> 00:21:29,420
What is this?

514
00:21:29,680 --> 00:21:30,980
Are you guys in a cult?

515
00:21:31,400 --> 00:21:32,220
What's the point?

516
00:21:32,380 --> 00:21:33,040
Smash brah.

517
00:21:33,740 --> 00:21:35,600
All the crew members thought we looked cool.

518
00:21:36,020 --> 00:21:38,340
Yeah, every employee here must have said hi to us.

519
00:21:49,340 --> 00:21:50,280
Wow, Tyda.

520
00:21:50,880 --> 00:21:52,660
Wow, Tyda? Screw you, man!

521
00:21:52,660 --> 00:21:54,660
Then why are you only looking at me?

522
00:21:54,660 --> 00:21:57,660
Hey! Let's all get a group picture for today!

523
00:21:57,660 --> 00:21:59,660
Yeah!

524
00:22:01,660 --> 00:22:04,660
Are you regretting not going all out and getting even weirder?

525
00:22:04,660 --> 00:22:06,660
I'm not.

526
00:22:06,660 --> 00:22:08,660
Okay, everyone look here!

527
00:22:08,660 --> 00:22:10,660
I'm heavy a little.

528
00:22:10,660 --> 00:22:12,660
Say cheese!

529
00:22:12,660 --> 00:22:14,660
We'll just have to come back.

530
00:22:14,660 --> 00:22:16,660
Yeah.

531
00:22:22,660 --> 00:22:28,660
Yeah! Hey!

532
00:22:28,660 --> 00:22:34,660
お決まりのフレーズは引き出しの中へ

533
00:22:34,660 --> 00:22:39,660
何よりも振り切って声を出してみる

534
00:22:39,660 --> 00:22:45,660
鏡の奥まで目を凝らして

535
00:22:45,660 --> 00:22:47,660
Ah! Take the good now!

536
00:22:47,660 --> 00:22:51,660
道を抜け言い合わせた影も

537
00:22:51,660 --> 00:22:55,660
曇る窓へ描くように

538
00:22:55,660 --> 00:22:57,660
縁取ってほしい

539
00:22:57,660 --> 00:23:01,660
言葉で透き通ったり

540
00:23:01,660 --> 00:23:03,660
縮む幻

541
00:23:03,660 --> 00:23:06,660
差し込めた日を踏んで

542
00:23:06,660 --> 00:23:12,660
跳ねた色も少しだけ好きになる

543
00:23:12,660 --> 00:23:21,660
ねえ 今を隠されちゃう前に

544
00:23:21,660 --> 00:23:27,660
意外な魔法をかけあって

545
00:23:27,660 --> 00:23:30,660
分からなくて

546
00:23:30,660 --> 00:23:34,660
分からないねって話して

547
00:23:34,660 --> 00:23:38,660
音頭が触った後に見つけた

548
00:23:38,660 --> 00:23:40,660
匂いが

549
00:23:40,660 --> 00:23:43,660
お目を見返しとってる

550
00:23:43,660 --> 00:23:53,660
お目を見返し

551
00:23:53,660 --> 00:23:55,660
お目を見返し

552
00:23:55,660 --> 00:23:57,660
お目を見返し

553
00:23:57,660 --> 00:23:59,660
お目を見返し

